   [38;5;179m# Firstmate instruction inbox[39m                                                                                                                                                                       [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mFirstmate steers you through durable message files in '<lab-home>/state/hscout.inbox'.[39m                                                                                                      [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mWhen a terminal message says an instruction is waiting there - and at any natural checkpoint when you are unsure - list them with `find '<lab-home>/state/hscout.inbox' -maxdepth 1 -name [39m  [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179m'*.msg' 2>/dev/null | sort -V`, read the complete contents of each record (including its final line even when it is not newline-terminated) and act on each message in numeric order, then [39m         [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179macknowledge each handled message by moving it: `mv '<lab-home>/state/hscout.inbox'/NNN.msg '<lab-home>/state/hscout.inbox'/handled/`.[39m                                               [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mPrefer the format-aware `fm_task_inbox_body` reader from `bin/fm-task-inbox-lib.sh` when it is available. If you read manually, a header line `body-terminator=1` means the writer added exactly [39m   [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mone synthetic final newline to terminate the record file; that marked newline is not part of the logical message body, so remove only it and preserve any intentional trailing newlines. Legacy [39m    [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mrecords without that marker may end without a newline; read them through the file end.[39m                                                                                                              [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mThe move IS the acknowledgement: without it firstmate rings again and eventually treats you as stuck. An empty or absent inbox needs no action.[39m                                                     [38;5;95m│
[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                       [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179m# Definition of done[39m                                                                                                                                                                                [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mWrite your findings to `<lab-home>/data/hscout/report.md`.[39m                                                                                                                                  [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mThe report must stand alone: what you did, what you found, the evidence (commands run, output, file:line references), and what you recommend.[39m                                                       [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mIf your deliverable is a visual artifact the captain will review and iterate on, use the lavish-axi rule: arm your board with bin/fm-procevent-lavish.sh arm <artifact.html> --for <task-id>; [39m      [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mnever run lavish-axi poll yourself. Re-arm with the reply after each nonterminal round to acknowledge it, route the board feedback through your steering inbox, write needs-decision [39m               [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179m[key=board-review] with the live board URL when the captain owes a decision, and stop at session_ended or an empty End without re-arming - acknowledge that final round with bin/fm-procevent.sh [39m   [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mhandled <source-id> <sequence> to conclude and retire your board.[39m                                                                                                                                   [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mBefore reporting done, read and follow `<worktree>/.agents/skills/captain-hold-lifecycle/SKILL.md` and pass its shared [39m         [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mcompletion gate for the report and any visual review.[39m                                                                                                                                               [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mOnly when the reviewed inventory is empty, run `FM_HOME='<lab-home>' bash '<worktree>/bin/fm-captain-hold.sh' complete[39m  [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179m 'hscout' --none`.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                  [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mThis exception permits only that command, not direct metadata edits, another task, or any backlog write.[39m                                                                                            [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mIf any captain call remains, ask firstmate to register the inventory and attest completion before you report done.[39m                                                                                  [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mIf the command refuses, report the refusal to firstmate and stop rather than bypassing the completion gate.[39m                                                                                         [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mWhen the report is complete, append `done [at=<epoch>]: {one-line conclusion}` to the status file and stop.[39m                                                                                         [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mIf your findings reveal work that should ship (e.g. you reproduced a bug and the fix is clear), say so in the report; firstmate may promote this task in place, and you would then receive [39m         [38;5;95m│
[39m   [38;5;179mmode-specific ship instructions as a follow-up message.[39m                                                                                                                                             [38;5;95m│
